includes: Tools → "Save to Apple Health" (off by default) writes the heart rate + respiratory rate Echoel itself measures (camera rPPG / BLE strap) into Apple Health. Safe by construction: non-circular (only self-measured sources, never echoes HealthKit/Watch data back), trustworthy units only (HR in BPM, respiratory in breaths/min; never writes HRV since our value is a 0..1 control, not real SDNN ms), throttled (>=15 s), range-guarded, availability-guarded. Decision logic is a pure unit-tested HealthWritePolicy; HKHealthStore calls isolated in HealthKitWriter. Uses the existing healthkit entitlement + existing NSHealthUpdateUsageDescription key (string corrected to truthfully describe the opt-in write). Plus everything from v10.34.3–v10.34.7. Verified: ci.yml (incl. HealthWritePolicyTests) + xcode-compile-check (AUv3 included) green through 78efa88.
